ArcLibre Printing disc
======================

This disc holds !Printers, the original Acorn printer manager, with its
three classes of printer, as in RISC OS 3.11: dot matrix, LaserJet and
PostScript. The printer driver modules they use are in !Printers: PDriver,
PDriverDP (dot matrix and LaserJet), PDriverPS (PostScript), PDumperSupport,
PDumperDM (dot matrix) and PDumperLJ (LaserJet). In RISC OS 3.11 !Printers
and the dot-matrix modules were in the ROM; ArcLibre ships them on this disc
to keep room in the ROM.

Printing
--------

Open this disc's directory viewer and double-click !Printers. Its icon
appears on the icon bar. Drag a printer definition from the PrintDefs
directory to that icon to install the printer: FX-80 (an Epson FX-80 dot
matrix printer), LasJet-II (an HP LaserJet II) or LW (an Apple LaserWriter,
a PostScript printer). Click Menu on the icon to configure it, choose where
its output goes (the parallel or serial port, or a file) and make it the
current printer. Applications such as Draw and Paint then print through it.

Copy !Printers and PrintDefs to a hard disc or another floppy to keep
them with your own applications.

This !Printers has no AUN remote printing (its modules are not published).
Nor does it have MakePSFont, the module that maps the desktop's outline
fonts to a PostScript printer's own fonts and downloads them: text in
outline fonts may not print correctly on a PostScript printer.

Licences
--------

!Printers, the modules and the printer definitions are Copyright 1996 Acorn
Computers Ltd and are distributed under the Apache License 2.0. !Printers'
BASIC is built from its pinned sources with the C preprocessor and the
ROM's own BASIC; the modules are assembled from their pinned sources. The
sources and full notices are in the ArcLibre source archive (src/PDriver,
src/PDModules, src/PDumperSpt, src/PDumpers, src/PrinterManager,
src/PrintDefs, src/MakePSFont, LICENSING.md).
